eight:583px;margin-top:4px;margin-bottom:4px;margin-left:12px;margin-right:12px;} .p21{margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:3px;page-break-inside:avoid;page-break-after:avoid;font-style:italic;font-size:14pt;color:#666666;} .p22{text-align:justify;line-height:1.4999500000000001;margin-top:13px;margin-inline-start:48px;orphans:2;widows:2;font-size:12pt;font-family:'PT Sans',sans-serif;color:#000000;} .i12{max-width:100%;height:auto;width:301px;height:381px;margin-top:4px;margin-bottom:4px;margin-left:12px;margin-right:12px;} .t15{font-size:13pt;} .p23{margin-top:15px;margin-bottom:3px;page-break-inside:avoid;page-break-after:avoid;font-weight:bold;text-decoration-line:underline;font-size:13pt;color:#1155cc;} .i13{max-width:100%;height:auto;width:2048px;height:1119px;margin-top:4px;margin-bottom:4px;margin-left:12px;margin-right:12px;} .i14{max-width:100%;height:auto;width:2048px;height:1150px;margin-top:4px;margin-bottom:4px;margin-left:12px;margin-right:12px;} .i15{max-width:100%;height:auto;width:1024px;height:669px;margin-top:4px;margin-bottom:4px;margin-left:12px;margin-right:12px;} .t16{font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;color:#222222;background-color:#ffffff;} .t17{font-size:10.5pt;font-family:'Roboto',sans-serif;color:#444746;background-color:#ffffff;} .i16{max-width:100%;height:auto;width:352px;height:349px;object-fit:cover;object-position:-6.428399999999999% -17.923724999999997%;margin-top:4px;margin-bottom:4px;margin-left:12px;margin-right:12px;} .i17{max-width:100%;height:auto;width:2048px;height:1536px;margin-top:4px;margin-bottom:4px;margin-left:12px;margin-right:12px;} .i18{max-width:100%;height:auto;width:2048px;height:1395px;margin-top:4px;margin-bottom:4px;margin-left:12px;margin-right:12px;} </style> </head> <body> <div class="doc-content"> <div class="section-break"></div> <h1 id="heading-h.bn0a9rlys6vo" class="title p1">State of Text Rendering 2024</h1> <h2 id="heading-h.hlkbwegonnpn" class="subtitle p2"><a href="https://behdad.org/text2024" class="t1"><u>behdad.org/text2024</u></a><span class="t2"><br>&#8203;</span><a href="https://behdad.org/" class="t3"><u>behdad</u></a><span class="t4"><br>&#8203;</span><span class="t5">8 July 2024</span></h2> <p class="p3">[Leave comments: <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1UnR2zKf3Z_DDRS6vLgBkSHUeqI3IGOEhWYh7rAIvsb8/view" class="t6"><u>Google Docs</u></a>, <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40911869" class="t6"><u>Hacker News</u></a>, <a href="https://lwn.net/Articles/981178/" class="t6"><u>LWN</u></a>, <a href="https://typo.social/@behdad/112754072201706886" class="t6"><u>typo.social</u></a>, <a href="https://x.com/behdadesfahbod/status/1810494842033820055" class="t6"><u>X</u></a>, <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/rust/comments/1e0dfj6/google_is_rewriting_harfbuzz_and_freetype_in_rust/" class="t6"><u>reddit</u></a>, <a href="https://www.phoronix.com/forums/forum/software/programming-compilers/1477212-the-state-of-text-rendering-2024-the-future-of-the-stack-with-rust" class="t6"><u>phoronix</u></a>]</p> <h1 id="heading-h.8qquqetupqvx" class="p4">License</h1> <p class="p3">This text is available under the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" class="t6"><u>Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike License 4.0</u></a>.</p> <h1 id="heading-h.wv1atmrlgdwn" class="p5">TL;DR</h1> <p class="p3">In this survey paper, I cover advances in the OpenType standard and the Open Source text stack and applications since 2009. I also discuss the future advances currently underway.</p> <p class="p3">In broad strokes, OpenType added support for <em>color fonts</em>, <em>variable fonts</em>, and the <em>Universal Shaping Engine</em>. The Free &amp; Open Source stack supports all of these advances at the lower level, but application UI support has been slower to arrive. The Open Source text stack also gained enormous market-share when Android and Google Chrome fully embraced it. Adobe now integrates parts of the Open Source stack for OpenType shaping in their flagship applications Photoshop, Illustrator and InDesign.</p> <p class="p3">Looking forward, there is a <em>Rust</em> migration of the text stack underway, which will unify font compilation and consumption under a safe programming language. <em>Incremental Font Transfer</em> will stream fonts to web browsers. And my proposed Wasm-fonts will finally enable correct rendering of the most complex writing systems that are not (and inherently can not be!) fully supported by the OpenType Shaping model, and more expressive fonts for simple writing systems like Latin.</p> <h1 id="heading-h.hb1bok4ov0gm" class="p4">Table of contents</h1> <div class="doc-toc"> <div class="toc-level-1"><p class="p6"><a href="#heading-h.8qquqetupqvx" class="t7"><u>License</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-1"><p class="p6"><a href="#heading-h.wv1atmrlgdwn" class="t8"><u>TL;DR</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-1"><p class="p6"><a href="#heading-h.hb1bok4ov0gm" class="t7"><u>Table of contents</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-1"><p class="p6"><a href="#heading-h.79cyqt2dmbbe" class="t8"><u>Preface</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-1"><p class="p6"><a href="#heading-h.ctas8s5ba95s" class="t7"><u>Dedication</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-1"><p class="p6"><a href="#heading-h.j80n2hwm7mxi" class="t8"><u>Prerequisites</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-1"><p class="p6"><a href="#heading-h.g6a0stcx9bs9" class="t8"><u>Introduction</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-1"><p class="p6"><a href="#heading-h.gyuunwknrd57" class="t7"><u>Looking back</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-2"><p class="p7"><a href="#heading-h.rxfoahh1rymb" class="t7"><u>OpenType</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-2"><p class="p8"><a href="#heading-h.rxfoahh1rymb" class="t7"><u>Color fonts</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-2"><p class="p8"><a href="#heading-h.rxfoahh1rymb" class="t7"><u>Universal Shaping Engine</u></a></p></div> <div class="toc-level-2"><p class="p8"><a href="#he